ComfyUI-AReA, experimental independent ComfyUI port, 2026.
Not an official release by the AReA authors or the ComfyUI team.

Contains modified source from:
AReA: Adaptive Receptive-Field Attention for Efficient High-Resolution Diffusion Transformers
Javad Rajabi, Koorosh Roohi, David B. Lindell, Babak Taati
https://github.com/KooroshRH/AReA
Commit: 9e38ec2d8457f2aa7800766e8a22d4960f160c69
License: Apache License 2.0 (included in LICENSE)

Modified upstream files (upstream path -> distributed path):
  area/attention.py -> area_core/attention.py
  area/bridge.py -> area_core/bridge.py
  area/schedule.py -> area_core/schedule.py
  area/tiling.py -> area_core/tiling.py
tiling.py uses ComfyUI's outer inference context and is invoked per image.
Changes include ComfyUI backend dispatch, independent batch statistics/layouts,
bounded window batching, bridge token bounds and phase/pooling validation.
adapter.py, nodes.py, saving.py, area_core/backend.py, area_core/__init__.py,
tests, release tools, documentation and annotated workflows are additions
for this port. The added source is also distributed under Apache-2.0.

ComfyUI API reference used during implementation:
https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI
